dhp377:1 starts: Shed passion
dhp377:2 starts: & aversion, monks–
dhp377:3 starts: as a jasmine would,
dhp377:4 starts: its withered flowers.
dhp373:1 starts: A monk with his mind at peace,
dhp373:2 starts: going into an empty dwelling,
dhp373:3 starts: clearly seeing the Dhamma aright:
dhp373:4 starts: his delight is more
dhp380:1 starts: Your own self is
dhp380:2 starts: your own mainstay.
dhp380:3 starts: Your own self is
dhp380:4 starts: Therefore you should
dhp380:5 starts: as a trader, a fine steed.
dhp384:1 starts: When the brahman has gone
dhp384:2 starts: to the beyond of two things,
dhp384:3 starts: then all his fetters
dhp384:4 starts: go to their end–
dhp388:1 starts: He’s called a brahman
dhp388:2 starts: a contemplative
dhp388:3 starts: one gone forth
dhp388:4 starts: for having forsaken
dhp396:1 starts: I don’t call one a brahman
dhp396:2 starts: for being born of a mother
dhp396:3 starts: He’s called a ‘bho-sayer’
dhp396:4 starts: if he has anything at all.
dhp396:5 starts: But someone with nothing,
dhp396:6 starts: who clings to no thing:
dhp399:1 starts: He endures–unangered–
dhp399:2 starts: insult, assault, & imprisonment.
dhp399:3 starts: His army is strength;
dhp399:4 starts: he’s what I call
dhp409:1 starts: Here in the world
dhp409:2 starts: –long, short,
dhp409:3 starts: large, small,
dhp409:4 starts: he’s what I call
dhp417:1 starts: Having left behind
dhp417:2 starts: having made his way past
dhp417:3 starts: from all bonds unshackled:
dhp417:4 starts: he’s what I call
dhp420:1 starts: He whose course they don’t know
dhp420:2 starts: –devas, gandhabbas, & human beings–
dhp420:3 starts: his effluents ended, an arahant:
dhp420:4 starts: he’s what I call
